From 462570a49ab3b1d34f1e2309dc632dcf32f6ac15 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 03:58:52 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] run_tests_parallel: report per-file peak RSS, warn
 on files over 512 MB
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Reap each per-file pytest child with os.wait4 and keep its ru_maxrss
(bytes on macOS, KiB elsewhere, normalized to bytes). The per-file time
distribution now prints the top 5 peak-RSS files beside the 10 slowest, and
one '⚠ high-memory test file' line per file over HERMES_TEST_FILE_RSS_WARN_MB
(default 512). Warning only: the exit code is unchanged. A file that needs the
memory on purpose raises its own threshold with a
'# run_tests_parallel: rss-warn-mb=<N>' line.

Why: tests/hermes_state/test_sidecar_keys_registry.py peaked at 1.58 GB per
run on the 16 GB Mac mini hermes_state lane for 3 days and nothing in CI
noticed (fixed in #655; example-card, example-card).
